// kama has no overloading, so a name is declared once per namespace — and for a GENERIC function
// nothing enforced that. `_generics[cName]` was a bare map assignment, so the second declaration
// silently replaced the first: this program built clean and returned 6, the LAST body's answer, with
// no diagnostic anywhere. A plain function at least died in the C compiler as a redefinition; this one
// was a wrong program that compiled.
fn T id<T>(T x) { return x; }
fn T id<T>(T x) { return x + x; }

fn int32 main() { return id(x: 3); }
